IMPORT prelude

-- Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974 (Singapore) -- the printing press licence and the printer's imprint (ss 3, 5, 6, 44(2)),
-- who may publish a newspaper and who may control a newspaper company (ss 7, 8, 10, 11, 12), the offences and defences for unapproved
-- control (s 17), foreign funding (s 19), newspaper permits, offshore and declared foreign newspapers (ss 21, 23, 24, 25, 28), the
-- register fees (s 31), possession offences (s 33), the general penalty (s 35), consent to prosecute (s 37) and composition (s 42).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/NPPA1974.txt, version in force
-- from 1 November 2022 (s 14 repealed by Act 31 of 2022 with effect from 1/11/2022; S 26/2022 annotated at s 39).
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 11 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the rules a printer, a publisher, an
-- investor in a newspaper company, a journalist or a seller of foreign newspapers actually meets. Not encoded: the Registrar and the
-- registers (ss 4, 29, 30, 32), approval criteria and objections as discretions (ss 13, 15, 16 beyond s 17's penalties), the
-- Registrar's information powers (s 18) beyond its penalty, search, seizure and examination powers (ss 26, 27, 34, 40, 41), the
-- management-share issue price (s 10(5), (6)), appeals to the President, and anything left to rules (fees, forms, which offences are
-- compoundable). "Substantial shareholder" takes its meaning from s 81 of the Companies Act 1967, which was not read: it is an input.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Newspaper and Printing Presses Act 1974`

§§ `3, 5, 6 and 44(2) -- printing presses and printed documents`

-- s 3(4): "A person must not keep for use or use any printing press without a licence." (5): "the occupier of any premises on which
-- any printing press is found is deemed to have kept it for use until the occupier proves the contrary." (6): a licence is
-- "ordinarily for one year". No penalty is stated in s 3; s 35 (general penalty) is the one that would apply -- an INFERENCE.
GIVEN `a press was found on the premises` IS A BOOLEAN, `the occupier proves the contrary` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the occupier is deemed to keep the press for use` IF
    `a press was found on the premises` AND (NOT `the occupier proves the contrary`)

GIVEN `keeps or uses a printing press` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a licence` IS A BOOLEAN, `the press is exempted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `keeping the press breaches s 3` IF
    `keeps or uses a printing press` AND (NOT `holds a licence`) AND (NOT `the press is exempted`)

-- s 44(2): "Nothing in this Act extends to the impression of any engraving or to the printing of any visiting or business card,
-- bill-head or letter heading."
-- s 5(1): "Every document printed within Singapore must have printed legibly on its first or last printed leaf the name of its
-- printer and publisher." "document" (s 2) means any printed newspaper, sheet, pamphlet, leaflet, map, chart and plan.
DECLARE PrintedThing IS ONE OF
    `a newspaper`
    `a pamphlet`
    `a leaflet`
    `a map`
    `a visiting card`
    `a business card`
    `a bill-head`
    `a letter heading`
    `an engraving`

GIVEN `the thing` IS A PrintedThing
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act extends to printing it` IF
    CONSIDER `the thing`
    WHEN `a visiting card` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a business card` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a bill-head` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a letter heading` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an engraving` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the thing` IS A PrintedThing, `printed in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it must bear the printer's and publisher's names` IF
    `printed in Singapore` AND `the Act extends to printing it` `the thing`

-- s 6: every printer must, "during 6 months from the date of the printing", keep one copy annotated with the name and residence of
-- whoever employed the printer, and produce it to a person authorised by the Minister. (Counted in whole months here; the boundary
-- day is not modelled.)
GIVEN `months since printing` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the printer must still keep a copy` IF
    `months since printing` LESS THAN 6

§§ `7 and 8 -- who may publish a newspaper`

-- s 7(1): Part 3 "applies to any newspaper published at intervals not exceeding one week unless the newspaper has been exempted".
-- s 8(1): such a newspaper "must not be published in Singapore except by a newspaper company"; (2) $50,000 or 3 years or both.
-- s 8(3): a newspaper is "deemed to be published outside Singapore if its contents and editorial policy are determined outside
-- Singapore and its sales or distribution are not intended primarily for Singapore".
GIVEN `days between issues` IS A NUMBER, `exempted from Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Part 3 applies to the newspaper` IF
    `days between issues` AT MOST 7 AND (NOT `exempted from Part 3`)

GIVEN `contents and editorial policy determined outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `sales intended primarily for Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the newspaper is deemed published outside Singapore` IF
    `contents and editorial policy determined outside Singapore` AND (NOT `sales intended primarily for Singapore`)

GIVEN `days between issues` IS A NUMBER, `exempted from Part 3` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `contents and editorial policy determined outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `sales intended primarily for Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `the publisher is a newspaper company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `publishing it is an offence under s 8` IF
        `Part 3 applies to the newspaper` `days between issues` `exempted from Part 3`
    AND (NOT `the newspaper is deemed published outside Singapore` `contents and editorial policy determined outside Singapore` `sales intended primarily for Singapore`)
    AND (NOT `the publisher is a newspaper company`)

§§ `10 -- management shares`

-- s 10(1)(a): all directors must be citizens of Singapore, (15) unless the Minister in writing approves a non-citizen.
GIVEN `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Minister's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be a director of a newspaper company` IF
    `is a citizen` OR `has the Minister's written approval`

-- s 10(1)(c): management shares "must not be issued or transferred except to citizens of Singapore or corporations who or which have
-- been granted the Minister's written approval"; (15) the Minister may approve a non-citizen. Read with "who or which", a citizen
-- also needs the approval -- an INFERENCE from the wording; s 10(2) likewise speaks of "any person who has been granted the
-- Minister's written approval".
GIVEN `has the Minister's written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `management shares may be issued to the person` IF
    `has the Minister's written approval`

-- s 10(4): on every subsequent issue of shares "1% of every such issue must consist of management shares".
GIVEN `shares in the issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`management shares required in the issue` MEANS
    `shares in the issue` TIMES 1 DIVIDED BY 100

-- s 10(11): a holder of management shares has "200 votes for each management share" on any resolution relating to the appointment or
-- dismissal of a director or any member of the staff, but "in all other respects the same voting rights as the holder of ordinary
-- shares". The votes per ordinary share come from the company's articles, not the Act: an input.
GIVEN `management shares held` IS A NUMBER, `votes per ordinary share` IS A NUMBER,
      `the resolution is on appointing or dismissing a director or staff` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`votes carried by the management shares` MEANS
    IF `the resolution is on appointing or dismissing a director or staff`
    THEN `management shares held` TIMES 200
    ELSE `management shares held` TIMES `votes per ordinary share`

§§ `11 and 12 -- control of a newspaper company`

-- s 12(3): a "12% controller" is a person who alone or with associates "(a) holds at least 12% of the shares ... or (b) is in a
-- position to control voting power of at least 12%".
GIVEN `percent of shares held with associates` IS A NUMBER, `percent of voting power controlled with associates` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a 12% controller` IF
    `percent of shares held with associates` AT LEAST 12 OR `percent of voting power controlled with associates` AT LEAST 12

-- s 12(4)(c): A is an associate of B if (i) A is "the spouse or a parent, step-parent or remoter lineal ancestor, or a son, stepson,
-- daughter, stepdaughter or remoter issue, or a brother or sister"; (ii)-(v) either is accustomed to act on the other's directions;
-- (vi) a related corporation; (vii), (viii) a corporation in which the other controls at least 20% of the voting power; (ix) a person
-- with whom there is an agreement or arrangement to act together. Cousins, uncles, aunts, nephews, nieces and in-laws are not listed.
DECLARE Relation IS ONE OF
    `a spouse`
    `a parent`
    `a step-parent`
    `a grandparent`
    `a son or daughter`
    `a stepchild`
    `a grandchild`
    `a brother or sister`
    `a cousin`
    `an uncle or aunt`
    `a nephew or niece`
    `a brother-in-law`
    `a related corporation`
    `a corporation 20 percent controlled by the person`
    `a corporation 15 percent controlled by the person`
    `a person who habitually follows the person's directions`
    `a party to an agreement to act together`
    `an unconnected fellow shareholder`

GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an associate` IF
    CONSIDER `the relation`
    WHEN `a cousin` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an uncle or aunt` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a nephew or niece` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a brother-in-law` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a corporation 15 percent controlled by the person` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `an unconnected fellow shareholder` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the relation` IS A Relation
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a family associate under s 12(4)(c)(i)` IF
    CONSIDER `the relation`
    WHEN `a spouse` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a parent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a step-parent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a grandparent` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a son or daughter` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a stepchild` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a grandchild` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a brother or sister` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- s 12(5): an "indirect controller" is a person (a) on whose directions the directors are accustomed or obliged to act, or (b) "who is
-- in a position to determine the policy of the newspaper company", but not (c) a director or other officer, (d) "a holder of any
-- management share", or (e) a person whose directions are followed "by reason only that they act on advice given by the person in
-- his or her professional capacity".
GIVEN `the directors act on the person's directions` IS A BOOLEAN, `can determine the company's policy` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `is a director or officer` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a management share` IS A BOOLEAN, `followed only as a professional adviser` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an indirect controller` IF
        (`the directors act on the person's directions` OR `can determine the company's policy`)
    AND (NOT `is a director or officer`)
    AND (NOT `holds a management share`)
    AND (NOT `followed only as a professional adviser`)

-- s 11(3): no agreement or arrangement "to act together" over voting shares "of an aggregate of more than 5% of the total votes"
-- without first obtaining the Minister's approval.
GIVEN `percent of votes covered by the agreement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the agreement to act together needs approval` IF
    `percent of votes covered by the agreement` GREATER THAN 5

-- ss 11(1), 12(1): a person must not, on or after 2 September 2002, become a substantial shareholder, a 12% controller or an indirect
-- controller "without first obtaining the Minister's approval". Whether the person becomes a substantial shareholder depends on
-- s 81 of the Companies Act 1967 (not read): an input.
GIVEN `becomes a substantial shareholder` IS A BOOLEAN, `becomes a 12% controller` IS A BOOLEAN, `becomes an indirect controller` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `percent of votes covered by the agreement` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Minister's prior approval is needed` IF
        `becomes a substantial shareholder`
    OR  `becomes a 12% controller`
    OR  `becomes an indirect controller`
    OR  `the agreement to act together needs approval` `percent of votes covered by the agreement`

§§ `17, 18, 19(7), 21, 24 to 26, 28, 33, 35 -- penalties`

-- s 17(1): contravening s 11, 12(1)(a) or (2)(a) [the 12% controller limbs] or 13(4)(a), (b) or (c)(i) -- fine up to $50,000, NO
-- imprisonment. s 17(2): contravening s 12(1)(b) or (2)(b) [indirect controller], 13(4)(c)(ii), 15(5), 16(2) or an approval condition
-- -- $50,000 or 3 years or both. Both add up to $5,000 a day for a continuing offence after conviction.
-- s 8(2) $50,000 / 3 years; s 18(3) $50,000 / 3 years; s 19(7) $50,000 / 3 years plus forfeiture of the funds; s 19(8) and s 21(9)
-- carry the s 35 penalty; s 24(5) and s 25(4) $50,000 / 2 years; s 26(5) and s 28(2) $5,000 / 6 months; s 33(1) $50,000 / 2 years;
-- s 35 (general) $50,000 / 2 years.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `publishing a weekly newspaper other than by a newspaper company`
    `becoming a substantial shareholder without approval`
    `becoming a 12% controller without approval`
    `becoming an indirect controller without approval`
    `disobeying a notice of objection`
    `disobeying a Minister's direction on shares`
    `ignoring the Registrar's information notice`
    `receiving foreign funds without approval`
    `a journalist not reporting foreign funds`
    `publishing a newspaper without a permit`
    `selling a declared foreign newspaper without approval`
    `reproducing a declared foreign newspaper without approval`
    `refusing to declare a declared foreign newspaper on entry`
    `subscribing to a declared foreign newspaper other than through an authorised distributor`
    `selling an unlawful newspaper`
    `any other failure to comply with the Act`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `refusing to declare a declared foreign newspaper on entry` THEN 5000
    WHEN `subscribing to a declared foreign newspaper other than through an authorised distributor` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 50000

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `becoming a substantial shareholder without approval` THEN 0
    WHEN `becoming a 12% controller without approval` THEN 0
    WHEN `publishing a weekly newspaper other than by a newspaper company` THEN 36
    WHEN `becoming an indirect controller without approval` THEN 36
    WHEN `disobeying a notice of objection` THEN 36
    WHEN `disobeying a Minister's direction on shares` THEN 36
    WHEN `ignoring the Registrar's information notice` THEN 36
    WHEN `receiving foreign funds without approval` THEN 36
    WHEN `refusing to declare a declared foreign newspaper on entry` THEN 6
    WHEN `subscribing to a declared foreign newspaper other than through an authorised distributor` THEN 6
    OTHERWISE 24

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the daily fine for a continuing offence` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `becoming a substantial shareholder without approval` THEN 5000
    WHEN `becoming a 12% controller without approval` THEN 5000
    WHEN `becoming an indirect controller without approval` THEN 5000
    WHEN `disobeying a notice of objection` THEN 5000
    WHEN `disobeying a Minister's direction on shares` THEN 5000
    WHEN `ignoring the Registrar's information notice` THEN 5000
    OTHERWISE 0

§§ `17(3) to (5) -- defences to unapproved control`

-- s 17(3): a defence to a s 11 or 12 charge to prove (a) the person "was not aware" of the contravention and (b) within 14 days of
-- becoming aware notified the Minister and took the action the Minister directed. s 17(4): for s 12(1) ONLY, also a defence though
-- aware, if (a) the contravention came from an increase in the holding of a family associate under s 12(4)(c)(i), (b) there is no
-- agreement or arrangement with that associate, and (c) the Minister was notified within 14 days of the contravention and the
-- directed action taken. s 17(5): "Except as provided ... it is not a defence ... to prove that the person did not intend to or did
-- not knowingly contravene".
GIVEN `was aware of the contravention` IS A BOOLEAN, `days taken to notify the Minister` IS A NUMBER, `took the action the Minister directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unawareness defence succeeds` IF
    (NOT `was aware of the contravention`) AND `days taken to notify the Minister` AT MOST 14 AND `took the action the Minister directed`

GIVEN `charged under s 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN, `the increase was by` IS A Relation, `has an agreement with that associate` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `days taken to notify the Minister` IS A NUMBER, `took the action the Minister directed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the family-increase defence succeeds` IF
        `charged under s 12(1)`
    AND `is a family associate under s 12(4)(c)(i)` `the increase was by`
    AND (NOT `has an agreement with that associate`)
    AND `days taken to notify the Minister` AT MOST 14
    AND `took the action the Minister directed`

§§ `19 -- funds from a foreign source`

-- s 19(5) "foreign source" includes (a) a foreign government or its agent; (b) a company, association or society constituted under
-- foreign law, branch in Singapore or not; (c) "any person who is not a citizen of Singapore whether or not the person is resident in
-- Singapore"; (d) a Singapore body with a non-citizen member or director that the Minister DECLARES by Gazette notification; (e) any
-- other source outside Singapore so declared.
DECLARE Funder IS ONE OF
    `a foreign government`
    `a foreign-incorporated company with a Singapore branch`
    `a permanent resident who is not a citizen`
    `a Singapore company with a foreign director, gazetted`
    `a Singapore company with a foreign director, not gazetted`
    `a Singapore citizen`

GIVEN `the funder` IS A Funder
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a foreign source` IF
    CONSIDER `the funder`
    WHEN `a Singapore company with a foreign director, not gazetted` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a Singapore citizen` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

-- s 19(1): a person must not receive "on behalf or for the purposes of any newspaper to which this Part applies any funds from a
-- foreign source without the Minister's prior approval"; (2) approval if the funds are "for bona fide commercial purposes";
-- (6) "Nothing in this section applies to any dealing by any person in the shares of a newspaper company quoted on a stock exchange in
-- Singapore."
GIVEN `the funder` IS A Funder, `has the Minister's prior approval` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a dealing in quoted shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `receiving the funds breaches s 19(1)` IF
    `is a foreign source` `the funder` AND (NOT `has the Minister's prior approval`) AND (NOT `is a dealing in quoted shares`)

-- s 19(3): unsolicited foreign funds must be reported to the Minister "within 3 days of the receipt".
GIVEN `days taken to report` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the unsolicited-funds report is in time` IF
    `days taken to report` AT MOST 3

-- s 19(8): a journalist who receives foreign funds "for printing or publishing any news item or article or for adopting a particular
-- line or bias" must report in writing "within 7 days to the managing director" of the newspaper company. (9): funds received from
-- outside Singapore by a journalist "are presumed to be from a foreign source unless proved to the contrary".
GIVEN `received from outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `proved not from a foreign source` IS A BOOLEAN, `days taken to report` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the journalist commits the s 19(8) offence` IF
    `received from outside Singapore` AND (NOT `proved not from a foreign source`) AND `days taken to report` GREATER THAN 7

§§ `21, 23, 24 and 28 -- permits and foreign newspapers`

-- s 23(7): "offshore newspaper" means a newspaper published outside Singapore [contents and editorial policy determined outside] "at
-- intervals not exceeding one week" with news or comment "relating to the politics and current affairs of any country in Southeast
-- Asia, except where the circulation of every issue of the newspaper in Singapore is less than 300 copies".
GIVEN `contents and editorial policy determined outside Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN, `days between issues` IS A NUMBER,
      `covers Southeast Asian politics and current affairs` IS A BOOLEAN, `largest Singapore circulation of an issue` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is an offshore newspaper` IF
        `contents and editorial policy determined outside Singapore`
    AND `days between issues` AT MOST 7
    AND `covers Southeast Asian politics and current affairs`
    AND `largest Singapore circulation of an issue` AT LEAST 300

-- s 21(1): no one may print or publish a newspaper in Singapore unless the chief editor or proprietor has a permit from the Minister;
-- (10) "This section does not apply to any offshore newspaper"; (2) no permit may be granted where publication "will constitute an
-- offence under section 8". (7) the permit is in addition to the s 3 press licence.
GIVEN `is offshore` IS A BOOLEAN, `has a permit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `printing or publishing breaches s 21` IF
    (NOT `is offshore`) AND (NOT `has a permit`)

GIVEN `publication would be an s 8 offence` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a s 21 permit may be granted` IF
    NOT `publication would be an s 8 offence`

-- ss 23(6), 24(6): a person found with "more than 5 copies of the same issue" of an offshore or declared foreign newspaper is
-- presumed, until the contrary is proved, to have them for sale or distribution.
GIVEN `copies of the same issue` IS A NUMBER, `rebutted` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is presumed to hold them for sale or distribution` IF
    `copies of the same issue` GREATER THAN 5 AND (NOT `rebutted`)

-- s 24(2): a person must not, without the Minister's prior approval, "sell or distribute or import for or possess for sale or
-- distribution any declared foreign newspaper". Possession for one's own reading is not in the list.
GIVEN `copies of the same issue` IS A NUMBER, `rebutted` IS A BOOLEAN, `sells or distributes` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Minister's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `dealing in the declared foreign newspaper breaches s 24(2)` IF
        (`sells or distributes` OR `is presumed to hold them for sale or distribution` `copies of the same issue` `rebutted`)
    AND (NOT `has the Minister's approval`)

-- s 28(1): "A person must not subscribe to any declared foreign newspaper except through a distributor who is authorised by the
-- Minister."
GIVEN `through an authorised distributor` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `subscribing breaches s 28` IF
    NOT `through an authorised distributor`

-- s 25(3): a person approved to reproduce a declared foreign newspaper "must not make any profit" but may recover "the cost of
-- production and services connected with the sale and distribution".
GIVEN `takings` IS A NUMBER, `cost of production and distribution` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the reproduction makes a forbidden profit` IF
    `takings` GREATER THAN `cost of production and distribution`

§§ `31, 33, 37 and 42 -- register fees, defences, consent and composition`

-- s 31: "$1 for every search and inspection"; "$2 for every copy" of a certified entry.
GIVEN `searches` IS A NUMBER, `certified copies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the newspaper register fee` MEANS
    `searches` TIMES 1 PLUS `certified copies` TIMES 2

-- s 33(1): publishing, selling or distributing an unlawful newspaper -- $50,000 or 2 years or both. (2): no conviction if the person
-- proves it was done "without the person's authority, consent and knowledge and without any want of due care on the person's part".
GIVEN `sold or distributed an unlawful newspaper` IS A BOOLEAN, `without authority, consent and knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN, `took due care` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be convicted under s 33(1)` IF
    `sold or distributed an unlawful newspaper` AND (NOT (`without authority, consent and knowledge` AND `took due care`))

-- s 37: "No prosecution may be instituted under this Act without the consent of the Public Prosecutor."
GIVEN `the Public Prosecutor consents` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a prosecution may be instituted` IF
    `the Public Prosecutor consents`

-- s 42(1): a PRESCRIBED compoundable offence may be compounded for "(a) a sum ... not exceeding $1,000 in the case of an offence
-- punishable on conviction with a fine not exceeding $5,000" or "(b) ... not exceeding $5,000" where the fine exceeds $5,000. Which
-- offences are prescribed is left to rules (not read): an input.
GIVEN `is prescribed as compoundable` IS A BOOLEAN, `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the most that may be collected to compound` MEANS
    IF `is prescribed as compoundable`
    THEN `the composition cap for a maximum fine of` (`the maximum fine` `the offence`)
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `fine` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the composition cap for a maximum fine of` MEANS
    IF `fine` AT MOST 5000
    THEN 1000
    ELSE 5000
